cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "hep-agentic-pipeline: an agentic LLM workflow for LHC new-physics reinterpretation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the foundational tools listed under references."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ammar
    family-names: Aziz
    email: ammarabdullahaziz@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  An agentic workflow that reinterprets a published ATLAS/CMS analysis against a user-specified
  new-physics model, running MadGraph -> Pythia8 -> Rivet/SimpleAnalysis -> pyhf to produce the
  signal-over-data overlay and a 95% CL exclusion limit. Validated against published acceptance x
  efficiency and exclusion limits with a tiered certification gate.
keywords:
  - high-energy physics
  - LHC reinterpretation
  - recasting
  - supersymmetry
  - agentic workflow
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ammarphp/ravel"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-30"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Reduce, Reuse, Reinterpret: an end-to-end pipeline for recycling particle physics results"
    authors:
      - family-names: Stark
        given-names: Giordon
      - family-names: Aristimuno Ots
        given-names: Camila
      - family-names: Hance
        given-names: Mike
    notes: "the mapyde package; arXiv:2306.11055; SciPost Phys. Codebases 27 (2024)"
  - type: software
    title: "Rivet"
    notes: "particle-level analysis framework"
  - type: software
    title: "pyhf"
    notes: "pure-Python HistFactory; public ATLAS likelihoods"
  - type: software
    title: "SModelS"
  - type: software
    title: "MadAnalysis 5"
